main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default template argument: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
could not be evaluated
--
The closure's function call operator was not marked constexpr, so the
constant evaluator did not evaluate its call: "expected constant
expression, but got '(unsigned int)plus_one(0)'" (also on develop).  In
libstdc++ 16, <format>'s __do_vformat_to lost its body through
__literal_encoding_is_unicode.
